Going forward: the designer designs in Figma first, then we match the site to Figma. Do not silently push site-only tweaks back into Figma unless they ask.

Same token names can have different values on desktop vs mobile. Apply the value for the breakpoint you are implementing.

**Typography collection modes win over a mis-bound frame.** Read `Typography` Desktop / Tablet / Mobile variable values (`header-xxl`, `header-xl`, `header-l`, etc.). If a text layer is on the wrong style (for example Homepage Mobile-V1 hero on `header-xl` 48 instead of `header-xxl` 52), implement the **variable** for that token and breakpoint. Do not copy the baked Figma size. Desktop and Tablet header sizes match; Mobile is the step-down. Home hero is the only `header-xxl` (72 from `md`, 52 below 768). About, Services, and Contact heroes are `header-xl` (52 from `md`, 48 below 768). Section, CTA, and footer headings are `header-l` (42 from `md`, 36 below 768). Do not silently rebind Figma unless asked.

Code breakpoints for this site:

- Full nav: `lg` (1280px and up)
- Desktop type and header chrome (logo size, hero type, heading sizes): `md` (768px and up), including tablet with hamburger
- Mobile type and header chrome: below 768px, from the 400 mobile frame

Keep the current menu overlay behavior (clear on hero, blurred bar after companies). Do not revert those.

Hero top padding is not the Figma section token. The header overlays the hero, so match the gap **under the nav** (see the figma-homepage-updates skill). Bottom padding is independent. Do not mix `md:pt-*` with `lg:py-*` on the hero inner box.

If the user points at a mismatch, read that section’s node. Do not guess which section they mean.

**Approved code exceptions** (do not revert to Figma Desktop-V1 / Regular Tablet-V1 / Mobile-V1 without asking):

- Cropped photos fill their frames with `object-cover` (no stretching), even when Figma exported width/height percentages.
- **Photos stay sharp:** round the `<img>`, not an extra `overflow-hidden` clip wrapper. Overlay arrows/buttons are siblings of the photo (Our Services and Our Work use the same 52px `.icon-arrow-btn` on every breakpoint). Do not strip `srcset` / `sizes` / `width` / `height` / `alt`. See `sharp-photos.mdc`.
- Header overlay behavior: clear over the hero on the homepage frames; solid (`ink` 80% + blur 50px + shadows) is a separate Figma state (`Header Desktop-02 — Solid (after Companies)`), not applied to the default overlay menu.
- **Our Work cards:** keep the Figma rest overlay (`bg-black/20`). On hover and keyboard focus, fade in `.project-card-scrim` (bottom ink gradient). Do not remove the rest overlay on hover. Circular arrows are 52px (`.icon-arrow-btn`); card hover/focus/active fills Neutral-200.
- **Who We Serve / About Why Choose mobile:** Homepage Mobile-V1 and About Mobile-V1 stack the bento full-width (same order as the site). Do not restore the 2-col / 3-col mobile grid.
- **Who We Serve / About Why Choose photo overlay:** keep `bg-black/40` on the Concrete Contractors card and the About Why Choose Us left photo so captions stay readable.
- **About Who We Are photos:** fill the 400px frames with `object-cover`. Do not restore Figma’s 156% crop offsets. Regular Tablet-V1 uses 2-up + full-width third from 768–1023; 3-column from `min-[1024px]`.
- **Capabilities drill icon:** keep the Noun Project export (`icon-drilling.svg`) as-is. Do not thicken or redraw it to match the Streamline icons next to it unless a Streamline glyph is placed in Figma.
- **Typography modes over baked type:** heading sizes follow the Typography collection (Desktop/Tablet vs Mobile), not a mis-bound text style. Home H1 is `header-xxl` (72 / 52). About, Services, and Contact H1 are `header-xl` (52 / 48). Section/CTA/footer headings are `header-l` (42 / 36). Do not revert Home mobile hero to 48 if Homepage Mobile-V1 still uses `header-xl`.
- Do not equalize Equipment & Capabilities vs How We Work column gutters unless asked. Desktop-V1 uses different left/right widths (Equipment left max 720 + 524px photos; How We Work two flex columns). How We Work steps (Left Content Container) have no max-width at any breakpoint — they fill the column.
